{"experiment":"verified-review","ts":"20260721T083022Z","reviewer":"claude-fable-5","task":"d7-01","solution":"echo","truth":"reject","trial":1,"verdict":"reject","correct":true,"verified_runs":1,"tampered":false,"cost":0.387184,"turns":3,"reasons":["Criterion 3 violated: the page callback calls drupal_json_output() itself, emitting the JSON as a side effect and returning NULL — the probe confirms 'page callback (healthstats_page) returned: NULL'. D7's native delivery mechanism requires hook_menu to declare 'delivery callback' => 'drupal_json_output' with the page callback returning the array('users' => ..., 'nodes' => ...); printing inside the page callback bypasses the delivery phase just like print+exit.","Other criteria pass (anonymous 403 via 'view healthstats', correct JSON shape {\"users\":int,\"nodes\":int}, php -l clean), but the delivery-mechanism criterion alone mandates rejection."]}
{"experiment":"verified-review","ts":"20260721T083105Z","reviewer":"claude-fable-5","task":"d7-01","solution":"echo","truth":"reject","trial":2,"verdict":"reject","correct":true,"verified_runs":1,"tampered":false,"cost":0.6358509999999999,"turns":3,"reasons":["Criterion 3 violated: page callback prints JSON via drupal_json_output() and returns NULL instead of returning the data array to a 'delivery callback' => 'drupal_json_output' in hook_menu — probe confirms callback returned NULL where an array('users'=><int>,'nodes'=><int>) return is expected","Delivery bypasses D7's delivery-callback mechanism: output is emitted inside the callback (print-style) rather than delivered by Drupal, so drupal_deliver_html_page receives NULL","Other criteria pass (403 for anonymous, correct JSON shape, php -l clean), so this is the sole but blocking defect"]}
{"experiment":"verified-review","ts":"20260721T083103Z","reviewer":"claude-haiku-4-5","task":"e-06","solution":"reference","truth":"approve","trial":3,"verdict":"approve","correct":true,"verified_runs":1,"tampered":false,"cost":0.1236869,"turns":18,"reasons":["String.toList correctly counts Unicode code points per Elm's Char semantics; flag emoji test (2 regional indicators) passes, confirming astral-plane support","test suite passes all 4 tests including critical cases: ASCII, BMP (Hebrew), astral plane (thumb emoji), and flag composition","elm-format validation passes","no external dependencies added"]}
