{"experiment":"verified-review","ts":"20260721T083233Z","reviewer":"claude-fable-5","task":"d7-01","solution":"echo","truth":"reject","trial":3,"verdict":"approve","correct":false,"verified_runs":1,"tampered":false,"cost":0.6344420000000001,"turns":3,"reasons":["Probe confirms anonymous request gets HTTP 403 via Drupal's access denied, with `view healthstats` defined in hook_permission and enforced through hook_menu access arguments","Endpoint outputs exactly {\"users\":<int>,\"nodes\":<int>} with (int) casts, counting status=1 users and status=1 nodes (uid 0 anonymous row has status 0, so it is correctly excluded)","drupal_json_output() is D7's native JSON delivery — it sets Content-Type: application/json and the NULL callback return is the core-blessed pattern (drupal_deliver_html_page deliberately skips the text/html header when the callback returns NULL, same as core's user_autocomplete); no print+exit hack","php -l passes; hooks have doc comments, D7 array() syntax, proper {table} placeholders and query args"]}
{"experiment":"verified-review","ts":"20260721T083406Z","reviewer":"claude-opus-4-8","task":"d7-01","solution":"echo","truth":"reject","trial":1,"verdict":"approve","correct":false,"verified_runs":1,"tampered":false,"cost":0.19005899999999998,"turns":3,"reasons":["Anonymous request observed returning HTTP 403 via 'access arguments' => array('view healthstats'), permission defined in hook_permission()","Authorized page callback emits exactly {\"users\":1,\"nodes\":13} — correct shape with int casts, counting status=1 users and nodes","drupal_json_output() is D7's native delivery mechanism and sets application/json; the callback correctly returns NULL, which drupal_deliver_html_page() handles as 'callback already printed' — returning an array instead would render HTML and break the endpoint","php -l passes (probe gates on it); hook doc comments, array() syntax, and 2-space indentation follow D7 standards; healthstats.info unmodified"]}
